# CHANGELOG.md merge=union
#
# Every pull request adds a bullet in the same place — the top of the
# section under [Unreleased] — so two branches cut from the same main
# collide there by construction, whoever wrote them. That conflict is
# where `fix/enricher-length-contract` entered this file: it is the tail
# of a `>>>>>>> ` marker that survived a hand resolution.
#
# `union` is one of git's built-in merge drivers: instead of stopping,
# it keeps the lines from both sides. For a file whose changes are
# additions, that is the right answer and removes the human from the
# resolution entirely.
#
# Known limit, worth remembering: union never honours a deletion. When
# one side removes a line and the other keeps it, the line survives.
# Removing something from this file therefore belongs in its own commit
# on main, not in a branch racing another one.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
